Depends: libc6 (>= 2.39), systemd, dbus, polkitd
Recommends: upower
Suggests: gnome-shell (>= 48)
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/hamishfor/predictive-battery-charging
Description: Predictive battery charging for Linux laptops
 Holds the battery below full while plugged in, and finishes charging shortly
 before you usually unplug, like macOS Optimized Battery Charging. It learns
 your routine from plug-in history, which stays on the laptop.
 .
 pbcd writes the kernel's standard charge-limit files on laptops with a
 matching hardware profile (ThinkPads to start with). On other laptops it only
 records charging activity. Includes the pbcctl command and a GNOME Quick
 Settings tile.
